# Model Profiles

## Why this exists

`ai.config.yaml` stores **runtime-agnostic** tiers (`quality`, `balanced`, `budget`). Each IDE (Cursor, Codex, Claude Code, …) names models differently and exposes different knobs. This file is the contract skills follow; optional concrete slugs live in `agents.runtimeModels` and `.ai/project.model-profiles.json`.

## Semantic tiers

| Tier | When to use |
|------|-------------|
| `quality` | Architecture, risky refactors, wide blast radius |
| `balanced` | Planning, orchestration main session, tracker, clarify |
| `budget` | Orchestrator review subagent, narrow checklists, reruns |

## Role → tier (from `ai.config.yaml`)

| Role | Tier |
|------|------|
| orchestrator | `{{ agent_model_orchestrator }}` |
| plan | `{{ agent_model_plan }}` |
| clarify | `{{ agent_model_clarify }}` |
| implement | `{{ agent_model_implement }}` |
| review | `{{ agent_model_review }}` |
| audit | `{{ agent_model_audit }}` |
| tracker | `{{ agent_model_tracker }}` |

## Runtime hints (optional)

If `agents.runtimeModels` is set, prefer the mapped slug when the active tool supports explicit model selection (e.g. Cursor Task `model` parameter). Example structure:

```json
{{ agent_runtime_models_json }}
```

When no mapping exists for the active runtime, **do not guess vendor IDs** — stay on the semantic tier and keep context lean per `.ai/reference/context-budget.md`.

## Multi-runtime rule

1. Read tier from `ai.config.yaml` for the skill role.
2. Load `.ai/project.model-profiles.json` if present (machine mirror after `sync` / `save`).
3. Apply runtime-specific slug only when executing in that runtime and the hint exists.
4. Orchestrator review subagent **must** use `budget` tier unless overridden.
5. Orchestrator **must** call `model-hint --role review` before review Task; optional audit only per `orchestrator.auditGate`.

## Editing

Change tiers in `ai.config.yaml` under `agents.modelTiers`. Add optional slugs under `agents.runtimeModels.<runtime>.<tier>`. Re-run project `sync` to refresh `.ai/project.model-profiles.json` and this reference.
